\p \v 4 \w Then the offerings|strong="H04503"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w and Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w will please|strong="H06149"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w as in days|strong="H03117"\w* \w of old|strong="H05769"\w* \w and years|strong="H08141"\w* \w gone by|strong="H06931"\w*.
\b 
\p \v 5 “\w Then I will draw near|strong="H07126"\w* \w to you|strong="H00413"\w* \w for judgment|strong="H04941"\w*. \w And I will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w a swift|strong="H04116"\w* \w witness|strong="H05707"\w* \w against sorcerers|strong="H03784"\w* \w and adulterers|strong="H05003"\w* \w and|strong="H07650"\w* \w perjurers|strong="H08267"\w*, \w against oppressors|strong="H06231"\w* \w of the widowed|strong="H00490"\w* \w and fatherless|strong="H03490"\w*, \w and against those who defraud laborers|strong="H07939"\w* \w of their wages|strong="H07916"\w* \w and deny justice|strong="H05186"\w* \w to the foreigner|strong="H01616"\w* \w but do not|strong="H03808"\w* \w fear Me|strong="H03372"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
\s1 Robbing God
\p \v 6 “\w Because|strong="H03588"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w*, \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w do not|strong="H03808"\w* \w change|strong="H08138"\w*, \w you|strong="H00859"\w* \w descendants|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Jacob|strong="H03290"\w* \w have not|strong="H03808"\w* \w been destroyed|strong="H03615"\w*. \v 7 \w Yet from the days|strong="H03117"\w* \w of your fathers|strong="H00001"\w*, \w you have turned away|strong="H05493"\w* \w from My statutes|strong="H02706"\w* \w and have not|strong="H03808"\w* \w kept them|strong="H08104"\w*. \w Return|strong="H07725"\w* \w to Me|strong="H00413"\w*, \w and I will return|strong="H07725"\w* \w to you|strong="H00413"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
\p “\w But you ask|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w How|strong="H04100"\w* \w can we return|strong="H07725"\w*?’
\p \v 8 \w Will a man|strong="H00120"\w* \w rob|strong="H06906"\w* \w God|strong="H00430"\w*? \w Yet|strong="H03588"\w* \w you|strong="H00859"\w* \w are robbing|strong="H06906"\w* \w Me|strong="H00853"\w*!
\p \w But you ask|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w How|strong="H04100"\w* \w do we rob You|strong="H06906"\w*?’
\p \w In tithes|strong="H04643"\w* \w and offerings|strong="H08641"\w*. \v 9 \w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w are cursed|strong="H00779"\w* \w with a curse|strong="H03994"\w*, \w yet you|strong="H00859"\w*— \w the whole|strong="H03605"\w* \w nation|strong="H01471"\w*— \w are still robbing Me|strong="H06906"\w*. \v 10 \w Bring|strong="H00935"\w* \w the full|strong="H03605"\w* \w tithe|strong="H04643"\w* \w into|strong="H00413"\w* \w the storehouse|strong="H01004"\w*, \w so that there may be|strong="H01961"\w* \w food|strong="H02964"\w* \w in My house|strong="H01004"\w*. \w Test Me|strong="H00974"\w* \w in this|strong="H02063"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*. “\w See if|strong="H00518"\w* \w I will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w open|strong="H06605"\w* \w the windows|strong="H00699"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H08064"\w* \w and pour out|strong="H07324"\w* for you \w blessing|strong="H01293"\w* \w without|strong="H01097"\w* \w measure|strong="H01767"\w*.\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Literally \fqa blessing for which there will be no room\f* \v 11 \w I will rebuke|strong="H01605"\w* \w the devourer|strong="H00398"\w*\f + \fr 3:11 \fqa The devourer \ft is probably a name for a crop-destroying pest.\f* for you, \w so that it will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w destroy|strong="H07843"\w* \w the fruits|strong="H06529"\w* \w of your land|strong="H00127"\w*, \w and the vine|strong="H01612"\w* \w in your field|strong="H07704"\w* \w will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w fail to produce fruit|strong="H07921"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
\p \v 12 “\w Then all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the nations|strong="H01471"\w* \w will call you blessed|strong="H00833"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w you|strong="H00859"\w* \w will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w a land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of delight|strong="H02656"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
\s1 The Book of Remembrance
\p \v 13 “\w Your words|strong="H01697"\w* \w against Me|strong="H05921"\w* \w have been harsh|strong="H02388"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*. “\w Yet you ask|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w What|strong="H04100"\w* \w have we spoken|strong="H01696"\w* \w against You|strong="H05921"\w*?’
\p \v 14 \w You have said|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w It is futile|strong="H07723"\w* \w to serve|strong="H05647"\w* \w God|strong="H00430"\w*. \w What|strong="H04100"\w* \w have we gained|strong="H01215"\w* \w by keeping|strong="H08104"\w* \w His requirements|strong="H04931"\w* \w and walking|strong="H01980"\w* \w mournfully|strong="H06941"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*? \v 15 \w So now|strong="H06258"\w* \w we|strong="H00587"\w* \w call the arrogant|strong="H02086"\w* \w blessed|strong="H00833"\w*. \w Not only|strong="H01571"\w* \w do evildoers|strong="H06213"\w* \w prosper|strong="H01129"\w*, \w they even|strong="H01571"\w* \w test|strong="H00974"\w* \w God|strong="H00430"\w* \w and escape|strong="H04422"\w*.’”
\p \v 16 \w At that time|strong="H00227"\w* \w those who feared|strong="H03373"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w spoke|strong="H01696"\w* \w with one|strong="H00376"\w* \w another|strong="H07453"\w*, \w and the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w listened|strong="H07181"\w* \w and heard them|strong="H08085"\w*. \w So a scroll|strong="H05612"\w* \w of remembrance|strong="H02146"\w* \w was written|strong="H03789"\w* \w before Him|strong="H06440"\w* \w regarding those who feared|strong="H03373"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w and honored|strong="H02803"\w* \w His name|strong="H08034"\w*.
\p \v 17 “\w They will be|strong="H01961"\w* Mine,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*, “\w on the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w when|strong="H00834"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w prepare|strong="H06213"\w* \w My treasured possession|strong="H05459"\w*. \w And I will spare|strong="H02550"\w* \w them|strong="H05921"\w* \w as|strong="H00834"\w* \w a man|strong="H00376"\w* \w spares|strong="H02550"\w* \w his own|strong="H05921"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w who serves|strong="H05647"\w* \w him|strong="H00853"\w*. \v 18 \w So you will again|strong="H07725"\w* \w distinguish|strong="H07200"\w* \w between|strong="H00996"\w* \w the righteous|strong="H06662"\w* \w and the wicked|strong="H07563"\w*, \w between|strong="H00996"\w* \w those who serve|strong="H05647"\w* \w God|strong="H00430"\w* \w and those who|strong="H00834"\w* \w do not|strong="H03808"\w*.”
\c 4
\s1 The Day of the LORD
\p \v 1 “\w For|strong="H03588"\w* \w behold|strong="H02009"\w*, \w the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w is coming|strong="H00935"\w*, \w burning|strong="H01197"\w* \w like a furnace|strong="H08574"\w*, \w when|strong="H01961"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the arrogant|strong="H02086"\w* \w and every|strong="H03605"\w* \w evildoer|strong="H06213"\w* \w will be stubble|strong="H07179"\w*; \w the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w is coming|strong="H00935"\w* \w when I will set them ablaze|strong="H03857"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*. “\w Not|strong="H03808"\w* \w a root|strong="H08328"\w* \w or branch|strong="H06057"\w* \w will be left|strong="H05800"\w* to them.”
\p \v 2 “\w But for you who fear|strong="H03373"\w* \w My name|strong="H08034"\w*, \w the sun|strong="H08121"\w* \w of righteousness|strong="H06666"\w* \w will rise|strong="H02224"\w* \w with healing|strong="H04832"\w* \w in its wings|strong="H03671"\w*,\f + \fr 4:2 \ft Or \fqa the Sun of Righteousness will rise with healing in His wings\f* \w and you will go out|strong="H03318"\w* \w and leap|strong="H06335"\w* \w like calves|strong="H05695"\w* \w from the stall|strong="H04770"\w*. \v 3 \w Then you will trample|strong="H06072"\w* \w the wicked|strong="H07563"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w they will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w ashes|strong="H00665"\w* \w under|strong="H08478"\w* \w the soles|strong="H03709"\w* \w of your feet|strong="H07272"\w* \w on the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w am preparing|strong="H06213"\w*,” \w says|strong="H00559"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*.
\b 
\p \v 4 “\w Remember|strong="H02142"\w* \w the law|strong="H08451"\w* \w of My servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w*, \w the statutes|strong="H02706"\w* \w and ordinances|strong="H04941"\w* \w I commanded|strong="H06680"\w* \w him|strong="H00853"\w* \w for|strong="H05921"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w at Horeb|strong="H02722"\w*.\f + \fr 4:4 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
\p \v 5 \w Behold|strong="H02009"\w*, \w I|strong="H00595"\w* \w will send|strong="H07971"\w* you \w Elijah|strong="H00452"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H05030"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the coming|strong="H00935"\w* \w of the great|strong="H01419"\w* \w and awesome|strong="H03372"\w*\f + \fr 4:5 \ft Or \fqa dreadful\ft ; LXX \fqa glorious\f* \w Day|strong="H03117"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*. \v 6 \w And he will turn|strong="H07725"\w* \w the hearts|strong="H03820"\w* \w of the fathers|strong="H00001"\w* \w to|strong="H05921"\w* \w their children|strong="H01121"\w*, \w and the hearts|strong="H03820"\w* \w of the children|strong="H01121"\w* \w to|strong="H05921"\w* \w their fathers|strong="H00001"\w*.\f + \fr 4:6 \ft Cited in Luke 1:17\f* \w Otherwise|strong="H06435"\w*, \w I will come|strong="H00935"\w* \w and strike|strong="H05221"\w* \w the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w with a curse|strong="H02764"\w*.”
